### 3. Implement `rateTicket`

- [ ] In `src/portal.js`, add `const { notifyAgent } = require('./notify');` after
  line 4, and add this function after `reply` (after line 28), then add it to the
  `module.exports` on line 30:

  ```js
  // The customer scores a resolved ticket once. A score of 1 or 2 emails the assigned agent.
  function rateTicket(store, customer, id, score, { now = new Date() } = {}) {
    const t = getMyTicket(store, customer, id);
    if (!t) return null;
    if (!Number.isInteger(score) || score < 1 || score > 5) throw new Error('score must be a whole number from 1 to 5');
    if (t.status !== STATUS.RESOLVED) throw new Error(`cannot rate a ${t.status} ticket`);
    if (store.getRating(id)) throw new Error('this ticket has already been rated');
    store.addRating(id, { owner_id: t.assignee_id, score, rated_at: now.toISOString() });
    if (score <= 2 && t.assignee_id) notifyAgent(store, t.assignee_id, { type: 'ticket_rated_low', ticketId: id, score });
    return store.getRating(id);
  }
  ```

  Update the export line to:
  `module.exports = { listMyTickets, getMyTicket, openTicket, reply, rateTicket };`

- [ ] Evidence: `npm test` — every test in `test/tickets.test.js` passes, including the
  seven new ones from step 2.

### 4. Commit

- [ ] `git add src/store.js src/portal.js test/tickets.test.js`
- [ ] `git commit -m "portal: add CSAT rating (store, rateTicket, low-score email)"`

## Exit criteria

- All of `npm test` passes.
- `src/portal.js` exports `rateTicket`; `src/store.js` exports `addRating`/`getRating`/
  `listRatings` from `createStore()`.
- Every acceptance criterion in `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` for requirements 1–4 has a
  passing test from step 2.

## Risks

- `getRating`/`addRating` key ratings by ticket id only (one rating per ticket, per the
  spec) — if a future spec change needs rating history, this shape needs revisiting;
  not a concern for this spec.
- The two reads of `t.assignee_id` in the new `rateTicket` function are exactly what
  phase 3's migrate step must find and update to `t.owner_id`.

